@* A row on its way, in the card's avatar: the ring the user watches with its
   percentage inside, and beside it the two verbs the table row keeps — watch the
   output, or stop it. Beside, not underneath: underneath they make the header
   taller than every other card's and the whole row of cards moves with it; at
   its side they only push the name along, and one over the other they take the
   width of a single button. A failed one keeps the ring in the error colour,
   says why in its tooltip, keeps the console when its output has the reason,
   and its cross becomes Dismiss, as the row does. One that ended well, for as
   long as it is still listed, has the ring whole and its cross in the success
   colour, as the row does. A project's ring, while a verb goes through its
   containers, is drawn in the two colours of its line (Mixed). *@

<div class="wslc-progress-ring @(Mixed ? "wslc-progress-mixed" : "")" title="@Status">
    @* A failed ring is drawn whole, as the row's bar is: at the percentage it had
       when it failed, often 0, there was no ring at all, only the mark inside it. *@
    @* Info, the blue of the "created" chip beside it: Primary sank into the dark header. *@
    <MudProgressCircular Class="wslc-progress-ring-dial" Color="@(Done ? Color.Success : Failed ? Color.Error : Color.Info)"
                         Indeterminate="@(Running && Pct <= 0)" Value="@(Running ? Pct : 100)" Min="0" Max="100">
        <MudText Typo="Typo.caption">@(Failed ? "!" : Done ? "100%" : $"{Pct}%")</MudText>
    </MudProgressCircular>
    @* The column is as tall as the ring; the magnifier sits at its top and the cross
       at its bottom (the stylesheet), as far apart as the ring allows. The cross is
       always the last one and always at the bottom, so when the magnifier goes —
       a run that failed after its pull — the cross does not move under the finger. *@
    <MudStack Row="false" Spacing="0" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Justify="Justify.FlexEnd" Class="wslc-progress-ring-verbs">
        @* No console, no button: an upload is bytes on their way, not output
           to read, and a magnifier that opens nothing is worse than none. *@
        @if (OnLog.HasDelegate && (Running || LogAfterFailure))
        {
            <MudIconButton Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Subject" Size="Size.Small" Color="Color.Info"
                           title="@LogTitle" aria-label="@LogTitle" OnClick="OnLog" />
        }
        <MudIconButton Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Close" Size="Size.Small" Color="@(Done ? Color.Success : Color.Error)"
                       title="@(Running ? CancelTitle : DismissTitle)" aria-label="@(Running ? CancelTitle : DismissTitle)" OnClick="@(Running ? OnCancel : OnDismiss)" />
    </MudStack>
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter] public int Pct { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The step under way, or why it failed.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string Status { get; set; } = "";

    [Parameter] public bool Failed { get; set; }

    /// <summary>It ended well and is still listed: drawn whole in the success colour, its cross closing it.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Done { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The work is a project's, some of its containers up and some not yet: drawn in both colours, the running one and the stopped one, as the line round its cards is.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Mixed { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Whether the console still has something to read once the row ended: a pull's output does, a run that failed after its pull has none.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool LogAfterFailure { get; set; } = true;

    [Parameter] public string LogTitle { get; set; } = "View pull output";

    [Parameter] public string CancelTitle { get; set; } = "Cancel pull";

    [Parameter] public string DismissTitle { get; set; } = "Dismiss";

    [Parameter] public EventCallback OnLog { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public EventCallback OnCancel { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The cross of a row that ended, well or badly: forget it.</summary>
    [Parameter] public EventCallback OnDismiss { get; set; }

    private bool Running => !Failed && !Done;
}
